      "reasoning": "Turn 4. Good - I killed Blood Aspirant and took 1 from the Familiar (18 life). I drew Phyrexian Rager - excellent card advantage! Opponent played Festering Newt and Goldvein Pick.\n\
\n\
Let me think about sequencing:\n\
- Play Swamp first (4 lands total: 2M, 2S)\n\
- Then I can cast Phyrexian Rager (2B) to draw a card and have a 2/2 body\n\
- Or Dance with Devils (3R) for two 1/1 devil tokens\n\
- Or Heartfire (1R, sac a creature) for 4 damage to opponent\n\
\n\
Phyrexian Rager is the best play — it draws me a card and adds a body. I should play the Swamp first, then cast Rager. I want to save Heartfire for later when I have devil tokens (sacrifice for damage + Heartfire for 4 more).",
