      "reasoning": "Opponent is attacking with Cauldron Familiar (1/1) and Festering Newt (1/1). I have Phyrexian Rager available to block.\n\
\n\
Key consideration: Festering Newt gives -1/-1 to target creature when it dies (or -4/-4 with Bogbrew Witch, which they don't have). If I block the Newt with Phyrexian Rager, the Newt dies and gives Rager -1/-1, making it a 1/1 — but it survives as a 1/1. Wait, in combat the Rager deals 2 to the Newt (killing it) and the Newt deals 1 to the Rager. So Rager takes 1 damage, then the Newt's death trigger gives it -1/-1 making it 1/1 with 1 damage on it — it dies!\n\
\n\
If I block Cauldron Familiar with Phyrexian Rager: Rager takes 1 damage, Familiar dies (but can come back with Food), and the Newt gets through for 1. But I keep my Rager.\n\
\n\
If I don't block: I take 2 damage (17 → 15).\n\
\n\
Best play: Block the Cauldron Familiar with Phyrexian Rager. Familiar dies (and doesn't seem to have Food to return), Rager survives, I only take 1 from Newt. But wait — if Newt dies to blocking, its trigger could kill my Rager.\n\
\n\
