      "seq": 72,
      "game_seq": 230,
      "reasoning": "They used Welding Sparks to kill my Phyrexian Rager! And the Festering Newt got through for 1 + seems to have gotten the Goldvein Pick equipped (now 2/2). But the Cauldron Familiar is in the graveyard without Food to return.\n\
\n\
Turn 5, I have 4 untapped lands and can play a 5th. Let me think:\n\
\n\
- Play Mountain (5th land), then cast Zurzoth (2R) = 3 mana, leaving 2 open\n\
- Or play Mountain, cast Dance with Devils (3R) = 4 mana, leaving 1 open\n\
- Or play Mountain, cast Havoc Jester (4R) = 5 mana, leaving 0 open\n\
\n\
Zurzoth is the strongest play — it creates Devil tokens when opponent draws on my turn, and has amazing synergy with the rest of my hand. I can play Mountain, cast Zurzoth for 3, and still have 2 mana open for Heartfire if needed!\n\
\n\
Wait, I should think about Havoc Jester too. It costs 4R and is a 5/5 — big body but no immediate impact. Zurzoth at 2/3 starts generating value immediately (devil tokens on opponent's draw step).\n\
