      "reasoning": "Opponent played Brazen Freebooter (3/3) which created a Treasure token, and another Festering Newt (1/1, sick). The equipped Festering Newt (2/2 with Goldvein Pick) is attacking.\n\
\n\
Should I block with Zurzoth? Zurzoth is 2/3, Newt is 2/2. Zurzoth would survive (takes 2, has 3 toughness) and kill the Newt. But when the Newt dies, its ability gives -1/-1 to one of my creatures until end of turn. If it targets Zurzoth, Zurzoth becomes 1/2 with 2 damage — it dies!\n\
\n\
Wait, let me check: Zurzoth takes 2 combat damage, then Newt dies and gives -1/-1 to a creature I control. If they target Zurzoth, it becomes 1/2 with 2 damage on it — that's lethal since damage equals toughness. Zurzoth dies.\n\
\n\
But the Newt has Goldvein Pick, so if it deals combat damage, opponent gets a Treasure. And the Newt will die to Zurzoth's 2 power anyway.\n\
\n\
If I don't block: I take 2 damage (16 → 14) and opponent creates a Treasure (from Goldvein Pick). But I keep Zurzoth alive for next turn's Devil generation.\n\
\n\
Keeping Zurzoth alive is more valuable than 2 life. I should take the damage.",
