      "game_seq": 396,
      "reasoning": "Wait — my Zurzoth and Slate Street Ruffian are in the graveyard! The opponent must have blocked during combat. Zurzoth died to something... Let me look at the board more carefully.\n\
\n\
The opponent's Festering Newt (1/1) and Brazen Freebooter (4/4) are attacking. They also played Dutiful Replicator (3/2, sick). \n\
\n\
I have Havoc Jester (5/5) and Devil Token (1/1) to block.\n\
\n\
Best blocking plan:\n\
- Block Brazen Freebooter (4/4) with Havoc Jester (5/5): Jester kills Freebooter and survives with only 4 damage. Excellent trade.\n\
- Let the Festering Newt (1/1) through for 1 damage. If I block Newt with Devil Token, the Newt dies and its trigger gives -1/-1 to one of my creatures, plus the Devil dies and pings for 1. But I'd rather save the Devil for Havoc Jester synergy.\n\
\n\
Actually, I could block the Newt with Devil Token: Devil Token dies (deals 1 to any target from death trigger), Newt also dies (its -1/-1 trigger goes... it has no good target if I also block Freebooter with Jester and Newt targets Jester, Jester becomes 4/4 with 0 damage — still fine).\n\
\n\
Wait — if I block both: Jester blocks Freebooter, Devil blocks Newt. Devil (1/1) vs Newt (1/1) = both die. Devil death trigger = 1 damage anywhere. Newt death trigger = -1/-1 to target creature I control. If they target Jester, it becomes 4/4 with 4 damage from Freebooter — it dies!\n\
\n\
That's terrible. If they can target Jester with the Newt trigger, I lose my 5/5.\n\
\n\
Better plan: Block Freebooter with Jester (5/5 vs 4/4), let Newt through for 1. Jester survives as 5/5 with 4 damage, I take 1 damage (14 → 13).\n\
\n\
But if Newt gets through unblocked, it doesn't die, so no Newt death trigger. Much safer.",
