      "game_seq": 435,
      "reasoning": "Three Devil tokens + Havoc Jester! I have 3 mana left and Heartfire in hand. Let me think about whether to Heartfire now or save it.\n\
\n\
Heartfire (1R): Sacrifice a creature, deal 4 damage to any target. If I sacrifice a Devil token, the Devil's death trigger deals 1 damage + Havoc Jester trigger deals 1 damage (from sacrificing) = 6 total damage to opponent if I target face! That's huge.\n\
\n\
But I could also just attack. Let me calculate the combat damage:\n\
- Havoc Jester (5/5) + 1 Devil Token (untapped, not sick) = 6 damage attacking\n\
- Opponent has Dutiful Replicator (4/3, sick) and Festering Newt (1/1, tapped) — nothing can block!\n\
\n\
So attacking gives 6 damage, putting them to 11. Then post-combat I can Heartfire sacrificing a Devil for 4 + 1 (devil death) + 1 (Havoc Jester) = 6 more damage, putting them to 5!\n\
\n\
Wait, that's amazing! But I should be careful — the sick Devil tokens can't attack. Only the original Devil Token is not sick. So:\n\
\n\
Attack: Havoc Jester (5) + 1 Devil Token (1) = 6 damage → opponent to 11\n\
Post-combat: Heartfire sac a Devil = 4 damage + 1 from Devil death trigger + 1 from Havoc Jester = 6 → opponent to 5!\n\
\n\
That's 12 total damage! But opponent is at 17, so 17 - 12 = 5. Can I go even further?\n\
\n\
Actually, Heartfire requires a sacrifice as additional cost. Let me save it for combat or post-combat. Let me head to combat.",
