      "game_seq": 449,
      "reasoning": "Wait — the Dutiful Replicator blocked my Devil Token! But it had summoning sickness... Oh wait, summoning sickness only prevents attacking, not blocking. The Replicator (4/3) blocks the Devil (1/1). The Devil will die and trigger 1 damage to any target + Havoc Jester doesn't trigger from the opponent killing my devil (only when I sacrifice).\n\
\n\
Actually wait — the Devil dies in combat, not from me sacrificing it. So Havoc Jester won't trigger. But the Devil's death trigger still fires: \"When this creature dies, it deals 1 damage to any target.\"\n\
\n\
Now, should I cast Heartfire here before damage? I could sacrifice another Devil token to Heartfire targeting the opponent's face: 4 damage from Heartfire + 1 damage from the sacrificed Devil's death trigger + 1 damage from Havoc Jester (I sacrificed a permanent!) = 6 damage. Plus 5 from Havoc Jester's combat damage + 1 from the combat Devil's death trigger = 7 more.\n\
\n\
Total: 6 + 5 + 1 = 12 damage? Wait let me recalculate.\n\
\n\
During combat (before damage):\n\
- Heartfire: sacrifice a sick Devil token → 4 damage to face + Devil death trigger (1 to face) + Havoc Jester trigger (1 to face) = 6 damage\n\
\n\
Then combat damage:\n\
- Havoc Jester hits unblocked → 5 damage\n\
- Devil Token blocked by Replicator: Devil dies → 1 damage from death trigger to any target (I can aim at face)\n\
\n\
So total: 6 + 5 + 1 = 12 damage. Opponent goes from 17 to 5.\n\
\n\
If I wait for post-combat: 5 from Jester + 1 from Devil death trigger = 6. Then Heartfire for same 6. Same total of 12.\n\
\n\
Actually, I should Heartfire now before damage so if opponent somehow has instant removal, I get maximum value. Let me do it!",
