  "annotations": [
    {
      "decision_index": 1,
      "player": "Opus Fate",
      "type": "blunder",
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Mulliganed a hand with 4 lands and a castable turn-2 play (Hobblefiend). While 2 of 3 spells need Black mana and there are no Swamps, the hand has a reasonable curve play and roughly 45%+ chance of drawing a Swamp by turn 3. In Limited, going to 6 cards is a significant cost.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to mulligan to 6",
      "better_line": "Keep the 7-card hand. Hobblefiend is a fine turn 2 play, you won't miss land drops, and you only need to draw one Swamp to unlock Slate Street Ruffian and Wight of Precinct Six.",
      "snapshot_index": 3,
    },
    {
      "decision_index": 2,
      "player": "Grok4 Story",
      "type": "blunder",
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Mulliganing a 6-card hand down to 5 is extremely punishing in Limited. While the hand has only one land (Swamp) and most spells require red mana, going to 5 cards drastically reduces the chances of winning. At 6 cards with a scry, there's roughly a 48% chance of finding a second land on the first draw, plus the scry helps. The hand has a reasonable curve if lands come (Sokenzan Smelter on 2, Malakir Familiar on 3, etc.).",
      "action_taken": "Mulliganed to 5 cards",
      "better_line": "Keep the 6-card hand and use the scry to look for a second land (especially a red source). One-land hands are risky but going to 5 in Limited is often worse.",
      "snapshot_index": 4,
    },
    {
      "decision_index": 45,
      "player": "Grok4 Story",
      "type": "blunder",
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Activating Blood Aspirant's ability to deal 1 damage to Slate Street Ruffian, which is summoning sick and cannot block this turn anyway. This will tap Blood Aspirant (removing it from combat), sacrifice Cauldron Familiar (losing a body), and spend 2 mana — all for 1 damage to a creature that wasn't threatening to block. The Ruffian survives at 2/1 equivalent.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Blood Aspirant's ability targeting the summoning-sick Slate Street Ruffian",
      "better_line": "Play Swamp, cast Festering Newt (B) and Goldvein Pick (2), then attack with Blood Aspirant and Cauldron Familiar for 2 unblockable damage since the Ruffian is summoning sick. This develops the board while dealing combat damage.",
      "snapshot_index": 61,
    },
    {
      "decision_index": 79,
      "player": "Grok4 Story",
      "type": "blunder",
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Festering Newt's death trigger would give Phyrexian Rager -1/-1, making it a 1/1 with 1 damage on it, killing it. Both creatures trade naturally without any spell needed. Welding Sparks (dealing 4 damage with 1 artifact) is premium removal being wasted to save a 1/1 Festering Newt.",
